Subject: [PATCH] Avoid indexing before an empty combo-box item

ConfigureDialog adds empty entries to several combo boxes at startup.
Reading str[str.length() - 1] then underflows the index and aborts with
libstdc++ assertions enabled. Check for an empty string before examining
its last character, preserving support for empty list entries.

--- a/src/combo/combo.cxx
+++ b/src/combo/combo.cxx
@@ -524 +524 @@
-	if (str[str.length() - 1] == '|') str.erase(str.length() - 1, 1);
+	if (!str.empty() && str.back() == '|') str.pop_back();
